\ ==== :modulation [ [ from to depth ] ... ], :carriers ====

\ Operator `from` adds depth x its output to operator `to`'s phase, in
\ radians. Operators are computed from the highest index down: a source with
\ a higher index than its target contributes this sample's output, any other
\ its previous sample's, so [ i i d ] is feedback. With a 1 kHz carrier and a
\ 100 Hz modulator at full level, the sidebands at 1000 + 100n Hz have the
\ amplitudes |Jn(depth)|.

11 seed

: settled ( stereo -- v ) | stereo | stereo 4800 48000 0 1 submatrix ;
: amp ( v hz -- a ) 48000 swap amplitude-at 0.70710678 / 10000 * round 10000 / ;
: voice ( patch -- v ) silence 0 patch! :a4 1 0 note-on 1 render-audio settled ;
: pm ( depth -- v ) | depth | { } [ { :fixed 1000 } { :fixed 100 } ] :operators ! [ [ 1 0 depth ] ] :modulation ! voice ;
: sidebands ( v -- ) | v | [ 1000 1100 900 1200 800 1300 700 ] ( v swap amp . ) each cr ;

\ === Bessel sidebands, discriminating against an additive sum ===
0 pm sidebands                  \ 1 0 0 0 0 0 0 (depth 0: the carrier alone)
1 pm sidebands                  \ 0.7652 0.4401 0.4401 0.1149 0.1149 0.0196 0.0196
2 pm sidebands                  \ 0.2239 0.5767 0.5767 0.3528 0.3528 0.1289 0.1289
3 pm sidebands                  \ 0.2601 0.3391 0.3391 0.4861 0.4861 0.3091 0.3091 (J0(3) is -0.2601)
clear

\ === routing: a chain 2 -> 1 -> 0 differs from 2 -> 0 and 1 -> 0 ===
{ :operators [ { :fixed 1000 } { :fixed 100 } { :fixed 30 } ] :modulation [ [ 2 1 1 ] [ 1 0 1 ] ] } voice to chain
{ :operators [ { :fixed 1000 } { :fixed 100 } { :fixed 30 } ] :modulation [ [ 2 0 1 ] [ 1 0 1 ] ] } voice to parallel
chain 1030 amp 0.001 < . parallel 1030 amp 0.1 > . cr          \ 1 1 (only the parallel form has a 30 Hz sideband at 1030)
chain parallel = . cr                                            \ 0
clear

\ === feedback: [ 0 0 d ] turns a sine into a harmonic series ===
: harmonics ( v -- ) | v | [ 2000 3000 ] ( v swap amp . ) each cr ;
{ :operators [ { :fixed 1000 } ] :modulation [ [ 0 0 0 ] ] } voice harmonics      \ 0 0
{ :operators [ { :fixed 1000 } ] :modulation [ [ 0 0 0.5 ] ] } voice 2000 amp 0.1 > . cr        \ 1
{ :operators [ { :fixed 1000 } ] :modulation [ [ 0 0 0.5 ] ] } voice 2000 amp
{ :operators [ { :fixed 1000 } ] :modulation [ [ 0 0 1 ] ] } voice 2000 amp < . cr              \ 1 (more depth, more harmonic)
clear

\ === carriers: which outputs are heard ===
{ :operators [ { :fixed 1000 } { :fixed 1500 } ] :carriers [ 0 1 ] } voice dup 1000 amp . 1500 amp . cr   \ 1 1
{ :operators [ { :fixed 1000 } { :fixed 1500 } ] :carriers [ 1 ] } voice dup 1000 amp . 1500 amp . cr     \ 0 1
{ :operators [ { :fixed 1000 } { :fixed 1500 } ] } voice dup 1000 amp . 1500 amp . cr                     \ 1 0 (default [ 0 ])
clear

\ === a modulator's level scales the index ===
{ :operators [ { :fixed 1000 } { :fixed 100 :level 0.5 } ] :modulation [ [ 1 0 2 ] ] } voice 1000 amp . cr   \ 0.7652 (J0(1): depth 2 x level 0.5)
clear
